cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "auto-eeg-analysis (AEA)"
message: "If you use this software in your research, please cite it as below. If you used a specific recipe, also cite the source paper declared in that recipe's citation.bib."
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Hou
    given-names: Dengzhe
    email: hou.dengzhe.t8@dc.tohoku.ac.jp
    affiliation: Tohoku University
repository-code: "https://github.com/dengzhe-hou/auto-eeg-analysis"
abstract: >
  AEA is an open library of EEG analysis skills for MNE-Python, with executable
  specifications and a numerically certified core. It provides shareable
  paradigm-specific recipes, automatic COBIDAS-MEEG methods-text generation,
  and a pre-submission reviewer-anticipation audit. EEGLAB and FieldTrip provide
  independent validation and selected alternative backend paths.
keywords:
  - EEG
  - electroencephalography
  - reproducibility
  - LLM agent
  - Claude Code
  - automated analysis
  - MNE-Python
  - EEGLAB
  - FieldTrip
license: MIT
version: 0.3.2
date-released: 2026-10-03
